hpc:ContentType a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .

hpc:OpenapiAssocsResp a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf hpc:ContentType .

hpc:AssociationDeleteResponse a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf hpc:OpenapiAssocsResp .

hpc:AssociationGetResponse a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf hpc:OpenapiAssocsResp .

hpc:AssociationPostRequest a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf hpc:ContentType .

hpc:AssociationPostResponse a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf hpc:OpenapiAssocsResp .

hpc:hasSchema a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain hpc:ContentType ;
    rdfs:range <#> .
```

This ontology fragment represents the classes `ContentType`, `OpenapiAssocsResp`, `AssociationDeleteResponse`, `AssociationGetResponse`, `AssociationPostRequest`, and `AssociationPostResponse`, and the object property `hasSchema`. The classes are subclasses of each other as indicated by the `rdfs:subClassOf` relations. The `hasSchema` property is used to relate a content type to its schema. The schema is represented by the `#` symbol, which is a placeholder for the actual schema definition.
